    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0209" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3181</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-01T10:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 1, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 2, 8.15
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>237. Greek Government announce concession of Entente that indispensable victuals
                    may be introduced pending the raising blockade. Entente allege large store
                    rifles not yet accounted for. Salute to flags Monday last.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[See telegram No. 4994, February 4, 1917 (received February 5, 8.30 p.m.),
                        from the Ambassador in Germany, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                            target="#pg114">page 114</ref>, for the following statement of peace
                        terms reported as made to the Ambassador by the Chancellor: <quote
                            rend="blockquote">
                            <p>Germany to give up Belgium but retaining so-called guaranties such as
                                railroads, forts, a garrison, ports, commercial control, etc.; a <pb
                                    facs="0210" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/> slice of France through
                                rectification of frontier; will only give back a small part of
                                Serbia, and Bulgaria can do as she likes with Roumania and everybody
                                must pay indemnities to Germany, etc.</p>
                        </quote>
                    </p>
                    <p>The Ambassador adds: “If Bernstorff
                        has given President any other terms he is fooling him, but do not quote me
                        to Bernstorff.”]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
